sec 7.4: timeliness reads each byte string on a line against its own author's retirement and retiring seq; the successor's handing off at seq 4, anchored at T+5, makes its own seq-3 entry timely, while the root's seq-2 entry on that line, above the root's retiring seq 1 and reached by no record earlier than the root's retirement at T+1, stays RETIRED: a gap at 2.
